IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-26: Article 26 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): obligations of deployers of high-risk AI systems.
-- Lines 491-512 of the consolidated text. Unchanged by the Omnibus. Article 2(13) names Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25, not Article 26: the gate (P3-section-3) gives Article 26 the same date and Art 2(2) tests as the others and never limits it under Art 2(13).
-- The party is the deployer (Art 3(4)); the keel decides who is one. Seams: Articles 13, 49, 71, 72 and 79(1) and the data protection impact assessment of Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 are plain BOOLEAN inputs named for the section they come from (Article 49 is S6's input; PLAN.md section 4 lists none of the others for this part); Article 25(1) and (3) say when a distributor, importer or product manufacturer is a provider.
-- "Without undue delay" has no number in the text and no deadline is encoded for it (fork F-undue-delay in NOTES.md). "Immediately" is the same day on a clock of whole days (fork F-immediately).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE met; JUST FALSE the duty applies and is not met; NOTHING not covered (the group does not yet apply, or the paragraph's own trigger is absent: limited by its own wording).
-- For a bar ("shall not use"): JUST TRUE the bar is on, JUST FALSE the "when" has not happened (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b) and the delegated-definitions ruling, item (c)); the two prohibitions of the third subparagraph answer NOTHING outside their own wording (fork F-bars).

DECLARE `Art 26 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 26(1) take appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure the system is used in accordance with the instructions for use`
    `Art 26(2) assign human oversight to natural persons who have the necessary competence, training, authority and support`
    `Art 26(4) ensure that the input data is relevant and sufficiently representative`
    `Art 26(5) monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use`
    `Art 26(5) inform providers in accordance with Article 72`
    `Art 26(5) inform the provider or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authority of the risk`
    `Art 26(5) suspend the use of the system`
    `Art 26(5) immediately inform the provider of the serious incident`
    `Art 26(5) then inform the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of the serious incident`
    `Art 26(6) cease to keep the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system`
    `Art 26(6) maintain the logs as part of the documentation kept pursuant to the relevant Union financial service law`
    `Art 26(7) inform the workers' representatives and the affected workers`
    `Art 26(8) comply with the registration obligations referred to in Article 49`
    `Art 26(8) use the high-risk AI system that has not been registered in the EU database`
    `Art 26(8) inform the provider or the distributor that the system has not been registered`
    `Art 26(9) use the information provided under Article 13 to comply with the obligation to carry out a data protection impact assessment`
    `Art 26(10) request an authorisation for the use of the post-remote biometric identification system`
    `Art 26(10) limit each use to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence`
    `Art 26(10) stop the use of the post-remote biometric identification system`
    `Art 26(10) delete the personal data linked to the use`
    `Art 26(10) use the post-remote biometric identification system in an untargeted way`
    `Art 26(10) document each use in the relevant police file`
    `Art 26(10) make each use available to the relevant market surveillance authority and the national data protection authority`
    `Art 26(10) submit the annual report`
    `Art 26(11) inform the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system`
    `Art 26(12) cooperate with the relevant competent authorities`

§ `Article 26(1): appropriate technical and organisational measures to use the system in accordance with the instructions for use`

-- src:493 | 1. Deployers of high-risk AI systems shall take appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure they use such systems in accordance with the instructions for use accompanying the systems, pursuant to paragraphs 3 and 6.
@ref Art 26(1) (src:493)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer has taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure it uses the system in accordance with the instructions for use accompanying the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(1) the deployer has taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to use the system in accordance with the instructions for use` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the deployer has taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure it uses the system in accordance with the instructions for use accompanying the system`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Deployers of high-risk AI systems shall take appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure they use such systems in accordance with the instructions for use accompanying the systems, pursuant to paragraphs 3 and 6"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

@ref Art 26(1) (src:493)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(1) the deployer's duty to take appropriate technical and organisational measures to use the system in accordance with the instructions for use` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(1) take appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure the system is used in accordance with the instructions for use`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "appropriate technical and organisational measures to use the system in accordance with the instructions for use were not taken"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)


§ `Article 26(2): human oversight assigned to competent natural persons`

-- src:494 | 2. Deployers shall assign human oversight to natural persons who have the necessary competence, training and authority, as well as the necessary support.
@ref Art 26(2) (src:494)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer has assigned human oversight to natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those natural persons have the necessary competence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those natural persons have the necessary training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those natural persons have the necessary authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those natural persons have the necessary support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(2) the deployer has assigned human oversight to natural persons who have the necessary competence, training, authority and support` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the deployer has assigned human oversight to natural persons` AND `those natural persons have the necessary competence` AND `those natural persons have the necessary training` AND `those natural persons have the necessary authority` AND `those natural persons have the necessary support`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Deployers shall assign human oversight to natural persons who have the necessary competence, training and authority, as well as the necessary support"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

@ref Art 26(2) (src:494)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(2) the deployer's duty to assign human oversight to natural persons who have the necessary competence, training, authority and support` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(2) assign human oversight to natural persons who have the necessary competence, training, authority and support`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "human oversight was not assigned to natural persons who have the necessary competence, training, authority and support"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)


§ `Article 26(3): paragraphs 1 and 2 are without prejudice to other deployer obligations and to the deployer's freedom to organise its resources`

-- A saving clause, not a duty: JUST TRUE for paragraph 1 or 2; any other paragraph is not named (NOTHING, silent).
-- src:495 | 3. The obligations set out in paragraphs 1 and 2, are without prejudice to other deployer obligations under Union or national law and to the deployer’s freedom to organise its own resources and activities for the purpose of implementing the human oversight measures indicated by the provider.
@ref Art 26(3) (src:495)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the paragraph` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(3) the obligations are without prejudice to other deployer obligations and to the deployer's freedom to organise its own resources and activities` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the paragraph` EQUALS 1 OR `the paragraph` EQUALS 2
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the clause names paragraphs 1 and 2 only
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

§ `Article 26(4): input data, to the extent the deployer exercises control over it`

-- src:496 | 4. Without prejudice to paragraphs 1 and 2, to the extent the deployer exercises control over the input data, that deployer shall ensure that input data is relevant and sufficiently representative in view of the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system.
@ref Art 26(4) (src:496)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer exercises control over the input data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the input data is relevant in view of the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the input data is sufficiently representative in view of the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(4) the deployer has ensured that the input data is relevant and sufficiently representative` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the deployer exercises control over the input data`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent the deployer exercises control over the input data" (the deployer does not exercise control)
        ELSE
             IF `the input data is relevant in view of the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` AND `the input data is sufficiently representative in view of the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that deployer shall ensure that input data is relevant and sufficiently representative in view of the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

@ref Art 26(4) (src:496)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer exercises control over the input data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(4) the deployer's duty to ensure that the input data is relevant and sufficiently representative` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the deployer exercises control over the input data`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(4) ensure that the input data is relevant and sufficiently representative`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the input data was not relevant and sufficiently representative in view of the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the deployer does not exercise control over the input data
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)


§ `Article 26(5), first sentence: monitoring on the basis of the instructions for use, and informing providers where relevant`

-- src:497 | 5. Deployers shall monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use and, where relevant, inform providers in accordance with Article 72. Where deployers have reason to consider that the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with the instructions may result in that AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), they shall, without undue delay, inform the provider or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authority, and shall suspend the use of that system. Where deployers have identified a serious incident, they shall also immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of that incident. If the deployer is not able to reach the provider, Article 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis. This obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data of deployers of AI systems which are law enforcement authorities.
@ref Art 26(5) first sentence monitor (src:497)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer has monitored the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(5) the deployer has monitored the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the deployer has monitored the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Deployers shall monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

@ref Art 26(5) first sentence monitor (src:497)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(5) the deployer's duty to monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(5) monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the operation of the high-risk AI system was not monitored on the basis of the instructions for use"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)


-- src:497 | 5. Deployers shall monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use and, where relevant, inform providers in accordance with Article 72. Where deployers have reason to consider that the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with the instructions may result in that AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), they shall, without undue delay, inform the provider or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authority, and shall suspend the use of that system. Where deployers have identified a serious incident, they shall also immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of that incident. If the deployer is not able to reach the provider, Article 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis. This obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data of deployers of AI systems which are law enforcement authorities.
