-- The second subparagraph: for a deployer that is a financial institution the monitoring obligation "shall be deemed to be fulfilled by complying with the rules on internal governance arrangements, processes and mechanisms pursuant to the relevant financial service law."
-- The deeming reaches "the monitoring obligation set out in the first subparagraph": read as the duty to monitor, not the duty to inform providers (fork F-26-5-deeming in NOTES.md; the other reading covers both).
-- src:498 | For deployers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law, the monitoring obligation set out in the first subparagraph shall be deemed to be fulfilled by complying with the rules on internal governance arrangements, processes and mechanisms pursuant to the relevant financial service law.
@ref Art 26(5) second subparagraph (src:498)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer complies with the rules on internal governance arrangements, processes and mechanisms pursuant to the relevant financial service law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(5) the monitoring obligation is deemed to be fulfilled` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF       `the deployer is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law`
             AND `the deployer complies with the rules on internal governance arrangements, processes and mechanisms pursuant to the relevant financial service law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For deployers that are financial institutions ..., the monitoring obligation ... shall be deemed to be fulfilled by complying with the rules on internal governance arrangements"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

§ `Article 26(5), second sentence: reason to consider that use in accordance with the instructions may result in a risk`

-- "without undue delay" carries no number; no deadline is encoded (fork F-undue-delay in NOTES.md), so no trace can show a breach.
-- src:497 | 5. Deployers shall monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use and, where relevant, inform providers in accordance with Article 72. Where deployers have reason to consider that the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with the instructions may result in that AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), they shall, without undue delay, inform the provider or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authority, and shall suspend the use of that system. Where deployers have identified a serious incident, they shall also immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of that incident. If the deployer is not able to reach the provider, Article 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis. This obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data of deployers of AI systems which are law enforcement authorities.
@ref Art 26(5) second sentence inform (src:497)
