§ `Article 26(5), third and fourth sentences: a serious incident, inform first the provider, then the importer or distributor and the authorities`

-- "immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities": the order is part of the duty. The function asks whether the provider was informed first;
-- the rule makes the provider's information due the same day and the second information due the same day as the first (fork F-immediately in NOTES.md).
-- src:497 | 5. Deployers shall monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use and, where relevant, inform providers in accordance with Article 72. Where deployers have reason to consider that the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with the instructions may result in that AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), they shall, without undue delay, inform the provider or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authority, and shall suspend the use of that system. Where deployers have identified a serious incident, they shall also immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of that incident. If the deployer is not able to reach the provider, Article 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis. This obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data of deployers of AI systems which are law enforcement authorities.
@ref Art 26(5) third sentence (src:497)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer has identified a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has informed the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has informed the importer or distributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has informed the relevant market surveillance authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider was informed before the importer or distributor and the market surveillance authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(5) the deployer has informed first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the market surveillance authorities, of the serious incident` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the deployer has identified a serious incident`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where deployers have identified a serious incident, they shall also immediately inform first the provider"
        ELSE IF       `the deployer has informed the provider`
                  AND `the deployer has informed the importer or distributor`
                  AND `the deployer has informed the relevant market surveillance authorities`
                  AND `the provider was informed before the importer or distributor and the market surveillance authorities`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they shall also immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of that incident"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- src:497 | 5. Deployers shall monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use and, where relevant, inform providers in accordance with Article 72. Where deployers have reason to consider that the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with the instructions may result in that AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), they shall, without undue delay, inform the provider or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authority, and shall suspend the use of that system. Where deployers have identified a serious incident, they shall also immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of that incident. If the deployer is not able to reach the provider, Article 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis. This obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data of deployers of AI systems which are law enforcement authorities.
@ref Art 26(5) third sentence (src:497)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer has identified a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(5) the deployer's duty to inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the market surveillance authorities, of the serious incident` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the deployer has identified a serious incident`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(5) immediately inform the provider of the serious incident`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE PARTY Deployer
               MUST `Art 26(5) then inform the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of the serious incident`
               WITHIN 0
               HENCE FULFILLED
               LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities were not informed of the serious incident after the provider"
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the provider was not informed immediately of the serious incident"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the deployer has identified no serious incident
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- "If the deployer is not able to reach the provider, Article 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis." An "If" that fails gives JUST FALSE (the periods ruling, rule (b)): this sentence does not bring Article 73 in.
-- What Article 73 then requires is outside this part (the function is a plain statement of the cross-reference).
-- src:497 | 5. Deployers shall monitor the operation of the high-risk AI system on the basis of the instructions for use and, where relevant, inform providers in accordance with Article 72. Where deployers have reason to consider that the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with the instructions may result in that AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1), they shall, without undue delay, inform the provider or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authority, and shall suspend the use of that system. Where deployers have identified a serious incident, they shall also immediately inform first the provider, and then the importer or distributor and the relevant market surveillance authorities of that incident. If the deployer is not able to reach the provider, Article 73 shall apply mutatis mutandis. This obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data of deployers of AI systems which are law enforcement authorities.
