§ `Article 26(6): keeping the logs, to the extent under the deployer's control, for at least six months`

-- Read as Article 19(1), which has the same words for providers: "to the extent such logs are under their control", an appropriate period of at least six months, "unless provided otherwise in applicable Union or national law" (the period is then that law's, outside the sources).
-- src:499 | 6. Deployers of high-risk AI systems shall keep the logs automatically generated by that high-risk AI system to the extent such logs are under their control, for a period appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system, of at least six months, unless provided otherwise in applicable Union or national law, in particular in Union law on the protection of personal data.
@ref Art 26(6) (src:499)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the deployer's control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer keeps the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period for which the logs are kept is appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months for which the logs are kept` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable Union or national law provides otherwise for the keeping of the logs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(6) the deployer keeps the logs for an appropriate period of at least six months` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the deployer's control`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent such logs are under their control"
        ELSE IF NOT `the deployer keeps the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Deployers of high-risk AI systems shall keep the logs automatically generated by that high-risk AI system" (the logs are under its control and are not kept)
             ELSE IF `the applicable Union or national law provides otherwise for the keeping of the logs`
                  THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless provided otherwise in applicable Union or national law, in particular in Union law on the protection of personal data"
                  ELSE IF `the period for which the logs are kept is appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` AND `the number of months for which the logs are kept` AT LEAST 6
                       THEN JUST TRUE
                       ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system, of at least six months"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- src:499 | 6. Deployers of high-risk AI systems shall keep the logs automatically generated by that high-risk AI system to the extent such logs are under their control, for a period appropriate to the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system, of at least six months, unless provided otherwise in applicable Union or national law, in particular in Union law on the protection of personal data.
@ref Art 26(6) (src:499)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the deployer's control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicable Union or national law provides otherwise for the keeping of the logs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(6) the deployer's duty to keep the logs for at least six months` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the deployer's control`
         AND NOT `the applicable Union or national law provides otherwise for the keeping of the logs`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         SHANT `Art 26(6) cease to keep the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system`
         WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the date asked` 6)) MINUS (Day `the date asked`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the logs were no longer kept before six months had passed"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the logs are not under the deployer's control, or other law provides otherwise
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

