§ `Article 26(10): post-remote biometric identification in the framework of an investigation`

-- The 48 hours: the rule below counts HOURS from the start of the use (hour 0), not days from the date asked. "ex ante, or without undue delay and no later than 48 hours": a request made before the use is represented as made at hour 0,
-- the earliest moment the trace can hold (fork F-26-10-ex-ante in NOTES.md). The exception, "when it is used for the initial identification of a potential suspect based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to the offence", takes the use out of the duty.
-- src:504 | 10. Without prejudice to Directive (EU) 2016/680, in the framework of an investigation for the targeted search of a person suspected or convicted of having committed a criminal offence, the deployer of a high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification shall request an authorisation, ex ante, or without undue delay and no later than 48 hours, by a judicial authority or an administrative authority whose decision is binding and subject to judicial review, for the use of that system, except when it is used for the initial identification of a potential suspect based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to the offence. Each use shall be limited to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence.
@ref Art 26(10) first subparagraph (src:504)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer uses a high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification in the framework of an investigation for the targeted search of a person suspected or convicted of having committed a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for the initial identification of a potential suspect based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has requested an authorisation, ex ante, or without undue delay and no later than 48 hours, by a judicial authority or an administrative authority whose decision is binding and subject to judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(10) the deployer has requested an authorisation for the use of the post-remote biometric identification system` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the deployer uses a high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification in the framework of an investigation for the targeted search of a person suspected or convicted of having committed a criminal offence`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the framework of an investigation for the targeted search of a person suspected or convicted of having committed a criminal offence, the deployer of a high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification shall request an authorisation" (no such investigation)
        ELSE
             IF `the use is for the initial identification of a potential suspect based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to the offence`
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except when it is used for the initial identification of a potential suspect based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to the offence"
             ELSE
                  IF `the deployer has requested an authorisation, ex ante, or without undue delay and no later than 48 hours, by a judicial authority or an administrative authority whose decision is binding and subject to judicial review`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the deployer of a high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification shall request an authorisation, ex ante, or without undue delay and no later than 48 hours, by a judicial authority or an administrative authority whose decision is binding and subject to judicial review, for the use of that system"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

@ref Art 26(10) first subparagraph (src:504)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer uses a high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification in the framework of an investigation for the targeted search of a person suspected or convicted of having committed a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for the initial identification of a potential suspect based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(10) the deployer's duty to request an authorisation for the use of the post-remote biometric identification system within 48 hours` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the deployer uses a high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification in the framework of an investigation for the targeted search of a person suspected or convicted of having committed a criminal offence` AND (NOT `the use is for the initial identification of a potential suspect based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to the offence`)
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(10) request an authorisation for the use of the post-remote biometric identification system`
         WITHIN 48
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "no authorisation was requested within 48 hours of the start of the use"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, there is no such investigation, or the use is for the initial identification of a potential suspect
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)


-- src:504 | 10. Without prejudice to Directive (EU) 2016/680, in the framework of an investigation for the targeted search of a person suspected or convicted of having committed a criminal offence, the deployer of a high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification shall request an authorisation, ex ante, or without undue delay and no later than 48 hours, by a judicial authority or an administrative authority whose decision is binding and subject to judicial review, for the use of that system, except when it is used for the initial identification of a potential suspect based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to the offence. Each use shall be limited to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence.
@ref Art 26(10) first subparagraph second sentence (src:504)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `each use is limited to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(10) the deployer has limited each use to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `each use is limited to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each use shall be limited to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

@ref Art 26(10) first subparagraph second sentence (src:504)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(10) the deployer's duty to limit each use to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(10) limit each use to what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "a use went beyond what is strictly necessary for the investigation of a specific criminal offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)


-- "If the authorisation requested ... is rejected, the use ... shall be stopped with immediate effect and the personal data linked to the use ... shall be deleted."
-- Stopping is due the day of the rejection (day 0 of the clock, "immediate effect": fork F-immediately); deleting has no deadline.
-- src:505 | If the authorisation requested pursuant to the first subparagraph is rejected, the use of the post-remote biometric identification system linked to that requested authorisation shall be stopped with immediate effect and the personal data linked to the use of the high-risk AI system for which the authorisation was requested shall be deleted.
@ref Art 26(10) second subparagraph (src:505)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the authorisation requested pursuant to the first subparagraph is rejected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of the post-remote biometric identification system linked to that requested authorisation has been stopped with immediate effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data linked to the use of the high-risk AI system for which the authorisation was requested has been deleted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(10) the deployer has stopped the use and deleted the personal data after a rejection` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the authorisation requested pursuant to the first subparagraph is rejected`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the authorisation requested pursuant to the first subparagraph is rejected"
        ELSE IF `the use of the post-remote biometric identification system linked to that requested authorisation has been stopped with immediate effect` AND `the personal data linked to the use of the high-risk AI system for which the authorisation was requested has been deleted`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the use of the post-remote biometric identification system linked to that requested authorisation shall be stopped with immediate effect and the personal data linked to the use of the high-risk AI system for which the authorisation was requested shall be deleted"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- src:505 | If the authorisation requested pursuant to the first subparagraph is rejected, the use of the post-remote biometric identification system linked to that requested authorisation shall be stopped with immediate effect and the personal data linked to the use of the high-risk AI system for which the authorisation was requested shall be deleted.
@ref Art 26(10) second subparagraph (src:505)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the authorisation requested pursuant to the first subparagraph is rejected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(10) the deployer's duty to stop the use immediately and delete the personal data after a rejection` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the authorisation requested pursuant to the first subparagraph is rejected`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(10) stop the use of the post-remote biometric identification system`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE PARTY Deployer
               MUST `Art 26(10) delete the personal data linked to the use`
               HENCE FULFILLED
               LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the personal data linked to the use was not deleted"
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the use of the post-remote biometric identification system was not stopped with immediate effect"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the authorisation was not rejected
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- "In no case shall such high-risk AI system ... be used for law enforcement purposes in an untargeted way, without any link to a criminal offence, a criminal proceeding, a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a criminal offence, or the search for a specific missing person."
-- JUST TRUE: the use is barred (for law enforcement, with no link to any of the four); NOTHING: not for law enforcement purposes, or a link exists (the prohibition limits itself in its own wording and the use falls outside the limit: ENCODING-GUIDE.md line 87; fork F-bars).
-- src:506 | In no case shall such high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification be used for law enforcement purposes in an untargeted way, without any link to a criminal offence, a criminal proceeding, a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a criminal offence, or the search for a specific missing person. It shall be ensured that no decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken by the law enforcement authorities based solely on the output of such post-remote biometric identification systems.
@ref Art 26(10) third subparagraph first sentence (src:506)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification is used for law enforcement purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is linked to a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is linked to a criminal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is linked to a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is linked to the search for a specific missing person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(10) the use is barred as untargeted` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification is used for law enforcement purposes`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "be used for law enforcement purposes in an untargeted way"
        ELSE IF       `the use is linked to a criminal offence`
                   OR `the use is linked to a criminal proceeding`
                   OR `the use is linked to a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a criminal offence`
                   OR `the use is linked to the search for a specific missing person`
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in an untargeted way, without any link to a criminal offence, a criminal proceeding, a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a criminal offence, or the search for a specific missing person" (there is a link: the use falls outside the prohibition's own limit; fork F-bars)
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- src:506 | In no case shall such high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification be used for law enforcement purposes in an untargeted way, without any link to a criminal offence, a criminal proceeding, a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a criminal offence, or the search for a specific missing person. It shall be ensured that no decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken by the law enforcement authorities based solely on the output of such post-remote biometric identification systems.
@ref Art 26(10) third subparagraph first sentence (src:506)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the use is untargeted: it is for law enforcement purposes and linked to no criminal offence, criminal proceeding, threat or search for a missing person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(10) the deployer's duty not to use the system in an untargeted way` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the use is untargeted: it is for law enforcement purposes and linked to no criminal offence, criminal proceeding, threat or search for a missing person`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         SHANT `Art 26(10) use the post-remote biometric identification system in an untargeted way`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the post-remote biometric identification system was used for law enforcement purposes in an untargeted way"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the use is not untargeted
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- "It shall be ensured that no decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken by the law enforcement authorities based solely on the output of such post-remote biometric identification systems."
-- JUST TRUE: the decision is barred; NOTHING: the decision has no adverse legal effect, is not taken by law enforcement authorities, or rests on more than the output ("solely": the prohibition limits itself in its own wording and the decision falls outside the limit: ENCODING-GUIDE.md line 87; fork F-bars).
-- src:506 | In no case shall such high-risk AI system for post-remote biometric identification be used for law enforcement purposes in an untargeted way, without any link to a criminal offence, a criminal proceeding, a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a criminal offence, or the search for a specific missing person. It shall be ensured that no decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken by the law enforcement authorities based solely on the output of such post-remote biometric identification systems.
@ref Art 26(10) third subparagraph second sentence (src:506)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the decision produces an adverse legal effect on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is taken by the law enforcement authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is based solely on the output of the post-remote biometric identification system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(10) the decision may not be taken` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the decision produces an adverse legal effect on a person` AND `the decision is taken by the law enforcement authorities`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken by the law enforcement authorities"
        ELSE IF `the decision is based solely on the output of the post-remote biometric identification system`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "based solely on the output of such post-remote biometric identification systems" (the decision rests on more than the output: it falls outside the prohibition's own limit; fork F-bars)
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

