§ `Article 26(11): informing natural persons subject to decisions made or assisted by an Annex III system`

-- "deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III that make decisions or assist in making decisions related to natural persons shall inform the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system."
-- The Annex III test reads the route in the `AI system` record (seam S1).
-- src:511 | 11. Without prejudice to Article 50 of this Regulation, deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III that make decisions or assist in making decisions related to natural persons shall inform the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system. For high-risk AI systems used for law enforcement purposes Article 13 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 shall apply.
@ref Art 26(11) first sentence (src:511)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer makes decisions or assists in making decisions related to natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has informed the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(11) the deployer has informed the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT ((`the AI system`'s `route` EQUALS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`) AND `the deployer makes decisions or assists in making decisions related to natural persons`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III that make decisions or assist in making decisions related to natural persons shall inform"
        ELSE IF `the deployer has informed the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall inform the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- src:511 | 11. Without prejudice to Article 50 of this Regulation, deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III that make decisions or assist in making decisions related to natural persons shall inform the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system. For high-risk AI systems used for law enforcement purposes Article 13 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 shall apply.
@ref Art 26(11) first sentence (src:511)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer makes decisions or assists in making decisions related to natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 26 act`
`Art 26(11) the deployer's duty to inform the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND (`the AI system`'s `route` EQUALS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`)
         AND `the deployer makes decisions or assists in making decisions related to natural persons`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 26(11) inform the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the natural persons were not informed that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the system is not an Annex III system, or the deployer makes no decision related to natural persons
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

-- "For high-risk AI systems used for law enforcement purposes Article 13 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 shall apply." A scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling, rule (c)): outside it, NOTHING.
-- src:511 | 11. Without prejudice to Article 50 of this Regulation, deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III that make decisions or assist in making decisions related to natural persons shall inform the natural persons that they are subject to the use of the high-risk AI system. For high-risk AI systems used for law enforcement purposes Article 13 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 shall apply.
@ref Art 26(11) second sentence (src:511)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the high-risk AI system is used for law enforcement purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(11) Article 13 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the high-risk AI system is used for law enforcement purposes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems used for law enforcement purposes Article 13 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 shall apply"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

§ `Article 26(12): cooperation with the relevant competent authorities`

-- src:512 | 12. Deployers shall cooperate with the relevant competent authorities in any action those authorities take in relation to the high-risk AI system in order to implement this Regulation.
@ref Art 26(12) (src:512)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the relevant competent authorities have taken an action in relation to the high-risk AI system in order to implement this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has cooperated with the relevant competent authorities in that action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 26(12) the deployer has cooperated with the relevant competent authorities` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the relevant competent authorities have taken an action in relation to the high-risk AI system in order to implement this Regulation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any action those authorities take in relation to the high-risk AI system in order to implement this Regulation" (no such action)
        ELSE
             IF `the deployer has cooperated with the relevant competent authorities in that action`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Deployers shall cooperate with the relevant competent authorities in any action those authorities take in relation to the high-risk AI system in order to implement this Regulation"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 26, "", 0)

